# Production Environment Variables Template

## For Backend (Render.com)
# Copy these to your Render dashboard when deploying backend

MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/todolist?retryWrites=true&w=majority
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=production

## How to get MongoDB Atlas URI:
1. Go to https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register
2. Create free M0 cluster (512 MB storage, free forever)
3. Create database user with password
4. Add IP address: 0.0.0.0/0 (allow from anywhere)
5. Get connection string and replace <username>, <password>, and database name

## For Frontend
# No environment variables needed - API URL is hardcoded in App.jsx
# After backend deployment, update VITE_API_URL in client/.env.production
